```console
$ scherzo-cloud workflow run --help
Run a local command and agent workflow

Usage: scherzo-cloud workflow run [OPTIONS] --source-root <ROOT> --execution-root <PATH> --run-dir <PATH> <WORKFLOW_FILE>

Arguments:
  <WORKFLOW_FILE>  Workflow definition path, resolved from the initial working directory

Options:
      --source-root <ROOT>
          Directory boundary for workflow source files
      --execution-root <PATH>
          Directory for workflow execution (must already exist)
      --run-dir <PATH>
          Directory to create for this run (must not already exist)
      --input-text <NAME> <TEXT>
          Supply one required named Text value
      --input-text-file <NAME> <PATH>
          Supply one required named Text value from a regular file, or - for standard input
      --input-attachment <NAME> <MEDIA_TYPE> <PATH>
          Append an immutable member to a named attachment collection
      --input-attachments-empty <NAME>
          Supply a present named attachment collection with no members
      --max-parallel <COUNT>
          Maximum simultaneous workflow steps [default: 1]
      --plain
          Force plain human presentation
      --json
          Print the result as JSON
      --color <WHEN>
          Select renderer color behavior [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help
          Print help

Interactive mode:
  Automatic mode uses the terminal interface only when stdin and stdout are terminals,
  TERM is usable, and stdin is not reserved by --input-text-file <NAME> -. Resize keeps the
  interface active; undersized terminals show a resize notice without changing modes.
  Use Up/Down or j/k to select steps, Enter to inspect logs, ? for complete help,
  Ctrl-C to request cancellation, and q to leave only after publication and cleanup.
  After q, Scherzo restores the terminal and prints the standard plain summary.

```
